<title>GERMANY: Waigel says fears of euro instability unjustified.</title>
<headline>Waigel says fears of euro instability unjustified.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>German finance minister Theo Waigel said on Saturday that fears of euro instability were unwarranted.</p>
<p>Asked about German fears that the euro, Europe's common currency, would not be sufficiently stable, Waigel said &quot;that fear is unjustified, the euro will be just as stable as the mark.&quot;</p>
<p>--Berlin Newsroom, +49 30 2039810</p>
</text>
